From: mscharged-port
Subject: Test desire update results as 32-bit codes
Upstream-base: 7a6bf165d9f1c5914181c079c7d4bfa7204f3509
Classification: TEMPORARY native source correction; remove when the pin includes decomp 0a6e72402.

FielderDesireMachine::Update and ScriptState::Update read the update result
through Variant's pointer member. Retail tests only the 32-bit word (R4QE01
lwz/cmpwi at 0x800D5BD8 and 0x80317568), and the result always holds an int
code (DESIRE_CONTINUE, 2 on timeout, ...), which ScriptMachine::Update reads
through mData.i. MWCC compiles both spellings to the same instructions.

Natively the pointer is eight bytes and the int assignment writes four. The
Windows (Clang) build copies stale stack bytes into the other four, so the
frozen state that hides a Strikers 101 or Striker Challenge team's missing
sidekicks ended at random moments and those sidekicks joined the match
(issue #25), and script states could skip their update. The Linux (GCC)
build happens to zero those bytes. Decomp commit 0a6e72402 fixes the source
with main.dol unchanged for R4QE01, R4QP01_rev2 and R4QP01_rev1; drop this
patch when adopting it.

diff --git a/src/Game/AI/FielderDesireMachine.cpp b/src/Game/AI/FielderDesireMachine.cpp
index fc1d493..b91d462 100644
--- a/src/Game/AI/FielderDesireMachine.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/AI/FielderDesireMachine.cpp
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ void FielderDesireMachine::Update(float deltaTime)
     {
         DesireUpdate result;
         UpdateStateMachine(frozen, &result, true, deltaTime);
-        if (result.mData.pointer != 0)
+        if (result.mData.i != DESIRE_CONTINUE)
         {
             RequestStateMachineDeactivation(frozen);
         }
diff --git a/src/Game/AI/shdStateMachine.cpp b/src/Game/AI/shdStateMachine.cpp
index be664c8..41a4887 100644
--- a/src/Game/AI/shdStateMachine.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/AI/shdStateMachine.cpp
@@ -274,7 +274,7 @@ bool ScriptState::Initialize(void*)
 void ScriptState::Update(
     DesireUpdate* update, float deltaTime)
 {
-    if (update->mData.pointer != 0)
+    if (update->mData.i != DESIRE_CONTINUE)
     {
         return;
     }
